1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,350
The Curiosity Club.

2
00:00:02,350 --> 00:00:04,741
Episode 25.

3
00:00:04,741 --> 00:00:07,065
The Clay Boat Rescue.

4
00:00:07,065 --> 00:00:09,782
Here is something to listen for.

5
00:00:09,782 --> 00:00:13,763
Did Maya need a different material to make the clay float?

6
00:00:13,763 --> 00:00:15,190
Ready?

7
00:00:15,190 --> 00:00:17,269
Let us find out.

8
00:00:17,269 --> 00:00:22,201
The science club has a small tub of water and a lump of modeling clay.

9
00:00:22,201 --> 00:00:25,788
Leo rolls the clay into a ball and drops it in.

10
00:00:25,788 --> 00:00:27,608
It sinks.

11
00:00:27,608 --> 00:00:31,508
Pip announces a rescue mission for the clay submarine.

12
00:00:31,508 --> 00:00:34,551
Maya takes the clay out and dries it.

13
00:00:34,551 --> 00:00:38,885
What if we change its shape without adding or removing any clay?

14
00:00:38,885 --> 00:00:42,513
She makes a wide little bowl with raised sides.

15
00:00:42,513 --> 00:00:46,576
When she places it carefully on the water, it floats.

16
00:00:46,576 --> 00:00:50,203
The material is the same, Leo says.

17
00:00:50,203 --> 00:00:52,921
So why is the result different?

18
00:00:52,921 --> 00:00:57,717
Ms. Park asks them to notice how much space the bowl shape takes up.

19
00:00:57,717 --> 00:01:00,692
Water pushes upward on objects.

20
00:01:00,692 --> 00:01:06,100
A floating boat displaces enough water for that upward push to balance its weight.

21
00:01:06,100 --> 00:01:12,649
The hollow shape keeps water out while allowing the boat to push aside more water before it is submerged.

22
00:01:12,649 --> 00:01:15,774
Leo puts a small block into the boat.

23
00:01:15,774 --> 00:01:17,771
It sits lower.

24
00:01:17,771 --> 00:01:20,855
He adds more, one at a time.

25
00:01:20,855 --> 00:01:25,163
Eventually, water comes over the edge and the boat sinks.

26
00:01:25,163 --> 00:01:30,054
Pip writes a passenger rule: Do not invite the entire classroom.

27
00:01:30,054 --> 00:01:34,769
They make a second boat with higher sides and compare the designs.

28
00:01:34,769 --> 00:01:41,032
They record their results instead of assuming that every wider or taller boat will always be better.

29
00:01:41,032 --> 00:01:44,429
At the end, Pip thanks the rescue team.

30
00:01:44,429 --> 00:01:48,464
The submarine has returned to boat life, he says.

31
00:01:48,464 --> 00:01:51,698
It has requested a smaller guest list.

32
00:01:51,698 --> 00:01:54,605
Now, a little more to discover.

33
00:01:54,605 --> 00:01:58,247
Water exerts an upward force called buoyancy.

34
00:01:58,247 --> 00:02:03,383
An object floating at rest displaces water whose weight matches its own.

35
00:02:03,383 --> 00:02:08,831
A boat's overall shape, including the space that keeps water out, matters.

36
00:02:08,831 --> 00:02:14,144
A material that sinks as a solid lump can be part of a floating hollow boat.

37
00:02:14,144 --> 00:02:16,983
Let us hear the main idea again.

38
00:02:16,983 --> 00:02:21,222
The same clay sank as a ball and floated as a hollow boat.

39
00:02:21,222 --> 00:02:26,127
Adding blocks made the boat sit lower until water came over the edge.

40
00:02:26,127 --> 00:02:31,752
The experiment connected shape, displaced water, and carrying capacity.

41
00:02:31,752 --> 00:02:34,728
Here are three useful expressions.

42
00:02:34,728 --> 00:02:37,853
You can listen, or say them with me.

43
00:02:37,853 --> 00:02:40,584
It is made of the same material.

44
00:02:40,584 --> 00:02:43,315
It is made of the same material.

45
00:02:43,315 --> 00:02:46,141
What happens if we change the shape?

46
00:02:46,141 --> 00:02:48,967
What happens if we change the shape?

47
00:02:48,967 --> 00:02:51,426
It sits lower in the water.

48
00:02:51,426 --> 00:02:53,885
It sits lower in the water.

49
00:02:53,885 --> 00:02:56,480
Remember our listening question?

50
00:02:56,480 --> 00:03:00,461
Did Maya need a different material to make the clay float?

51
00:03:00,461 --> 00:03:02,595
Here is the answer.

52
00:03:02,595 --> 00:03:04,076
No.

53
00:03:04,076 --> 00:03:10,013
She changed the shape into a hollow boat that could displace enough water while keeping water out.

54
00:03:10,013 --> 00:03:13,668
And here is a question just for your imagination.

55
00:03:13,668 --> 00:03:18,804
What features would you try in a model boat that has to carry a few small blocks?

56
00:03:18,804 --> 00:03:21,915
There is more than one possible answer.

57
00:03:21,915 --> 00:03:25,163
Keep wondering, and see you next time.
